🇺🇸🇮🇷Regarding Reports of Empty US Stockpiles

▪️Yes, stockpiles are likely low, including of ATACMS and PrSM missiles (the newer, longer-range replacement for ATACMS) - as well as anti-missile munitions;

▪️However all of these munitions are under production, PrSM missile are made 10 per month with an eventual peak production rate of 30+ per month sometime next year;

▪️This is why the US strikes Iran, plays "diplomacy" games, then strikes again - to refill stockpiles enough for the next round of operations;

▪️ As production ramps up - howerever lower rates may be than say Russia or China - the intensity of these intermittent strikes will increase;

▪️Iran and its allies will (and likely are) factoring that into their strategies;

▪️The outlook will be prolonged on/off conflict pitting the US capacity to wear Iran down against Iran's capacity to weather military aggression (along with economic pressure and subversion) long enough for multipolarism to fully displace US unipolarism and neutralize the threat it poses to Iran and the rest of the world (including the American people);

